# Temporary ignore — remove once Alpine publishes the patched openssl/libssl3/libcrypto3
# build (3.5.8-r0) to the apk repo the eclipse-temurin:17-jre-alpine base image pulls from.
#
# The Dockerfile already runs `apk upgrade --no-cache` specifically to pick up fixed OS
# packages before Trivy scans the built image (see the Dockerfile's own comment), but that
# only helps once the fix is actually published upstream. As of 2026-08-26, Trivy's vulnerability
# DB already lists a fix (3.5.8-r0) but Alpine 3.24's apk repo still only serves 3.5.7-r0 —
# confirmed via two identical CI failures on skillars-deferred-69's PR #107, ~10 minutes apart,
# both installed-version 3.5.7-r0. Added by skillars-deferred-70 story-creation with the project
# owner's explicit sign-off (2026-08-26), scoped to this one CVE only, not a blanket suppression.
#
# openssl: OpenSSL: Denial of Service via unbounded memory growth in QUIC server
CVE-2026-14456
